<p>Probably not, actually.</p>
<p>Look, this thing claims that its rotating brush head (capable of 350 rpm) and its amazing torque allow it to blast away calcium, mold, grease, mildew, and all sorts of other stuff. The <a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0CPH4PYTP?lv=shuf&channelId=500&plpRedirect=mhFallback&th=1&tag=mehdown-20#averageCustomerReviewsAnchor">Amazon reviews back this up somewhat</a>, but a) they’re not always reliable, and b) there are some naysayers.</p>
<p>Which is why we’re selling it for $20.</p>
<p>Were we charging the 50 bucks this thing goes for on Amazon, it would be too risky. That’s more than you want to spend on something that might not live up to its ridiculous promises. 20 dollars, meanwhile, is the perfect price for something that will likely be useful, if not slightly less useful than it claims.</p>
<p>Also: it looks pretty ridiculous and fun to use. So there’s that too.</p>
